like to trade the FTB to the FL, and the break of the flag after price returns to it (after it has filled the pole base).\n\nto trade the engulf of the FL would require a few things - that the further FL point is a reaction to something significant. - and also that it gives me a clear place like an FTR or such to base a trade on.\n\npedini and sunny do that a lot in their journals with good success btw, so they are more experienced in this matter. not all structures are good for such a trade but they find good ones and they work for them\n\nbtw, if you have specific example post it and we can discuss it","a":"—","d":"","n":"#715","p":29,"im":[],"m":715},{"id":"flaglimits_p29_716","t":"Hello All,\n\nHere is my first attempt at the homework for the flag limits. Thanks!","a":"—","d":"","n":"#716","p":29,"im":["3d2e37e19893f4bda3492a680eb6433d25d8ded8","c94e41a55a8bced8b2945f7e2e08fd073ba731f7","e0096c1c682e0ae5c9f32eae2d3dfcf7311f7e58"],"m":716},{"id":"flaglimits_p29_717","t":"Hi Pedini! Just a few questions: i made some remarks on FL chart from marketpedia. Let me see if i understand correctly:\n\n1) a PAZ its a space between two FL/FTR(compression is a PAZ, FLAG its a Stacked S/D i dont understand how i can consider a paz ) Now, inside a FLAG (PAZ) we can have another FLAGS with their FLs. Fl itself is a FLAG with its FL. How you look correctly for a range and its FL? For compression its clear but for FLAG not. 2) if price break into a PAZ it want to go to the other side of the PAZ.\n\nFl which define other small flag inside our flag can also act as FTA im alright? How you can see that? There is a video. I think i explained much better there. I hope:D\n\nPedini wrote: Hiya Wes. The circle you have marked is a FL. It tells us that price is happy to range below that level until it breaks. When it breaks, it sends the signal that price will continue higher.\n\nPeds","a":"—","d":"","n":"#717","p":29,"im":["4c33327729177bdfabf68e94ca682672851bc33f"],"m":717},{"id":"flagli